-- Q170: Equity [easy/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Both alternatives produce identical effects on equity components since the economic outcome of doubling shares is the same","The stock split halves par to $1 with no journal entry, while the 100% stock dividend transfers $200,000 from retained earnings to common stock at par","The stock split reduces retained earnings by $200,000 while the stock dividend requires no retained earnings transfer under ASC 505","Both alternatives transfer $200,000 from retained earnings, but the split uses par value while the dividend uses fair market value"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): A 2-for-1 stock split doubles shares to 200,000 and halves par to $1 with no journal entry — only a memo notation. A 100% large stock dividend (ASC 505-20-25-4) requires a debit to retained earnings at par: $200,000 transferred to common stock. The split leaves all equity components unchanged; the dividend reduces retained earnings by $200,000.
Wrong (A): The stock dividend requires a retained earnings transfer of $200,000, so the effects are not identical.
Wrong (C): This reverses the treatment — it is the dividend, not the split, that reduces retained earnings.
Wrong (D): Large stock dividends use par value, not fair market value; fair value applies only to small stock dividends (under 20-25%).$EXPL$
