-- Q11659: Accounting Changes and Error Corrections [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["The auditor''s opinion on the reasonableness of the new accounting estimate","The nature of the change and its effect on income, net income, and related per-share amounts","The indirect effects of the estimate change on the entity''s projected future cash flows","A detailed reconciliation of the old and new estimation methodologies used"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): ASC 250-10-50-4 requires disclosure of the nature of a material estimate change and its effect on income from continuing operations, net income, and related per-share amounts. If the change affects future periods, that fact must also be disclosed when estimable.
Wrong (A): The auditor''s opinion on the estimate is not a required disclosure element under ASC 250.
Wrong (C): ASC 250 requires disclosure of the effect on reported amounts, not indirect effects on future cash flows.
