-- Q11662: Accounting Changes and Error Corrections [medium/L3]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Retrospectively restate all prior periods to remove previously recognized equity method income","Continue applying the equity method until the investment is ultimately sold or disposed of","Prospectively cease the equity method and carry the investment at its book value as of the change date","Write the investment down to zero and recognize an immediate loss on the income statement"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under ASC 323-10-35-36 and ASC 250-10-45-17, when an investor loses significant influence due to dilution, it ceases the equity method prospectively. The investment retains its equity-method carrying amount at the change date and is subsequently accounted for under ASC 321.
Wrong (A): This results from changed circumstances, not a voluntary accounting principle change — retrospective restatement is not required.
Wrong (B): The equity method must cease when significant influence is lost; continuing it would overstate the investor''s influence.
Wrong (D): The investment is not written to zero — it is carried at its existing equity-method book value.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 11662;

