-- Q11704: Contingencies [hard/L4]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Adjust goodwill by reducing it $500,000 to reflect the revised contingent consideration estimate","Recognize a $500,000 gain in earnings because the liability is remeasured at fair value each period","Retain the original $1,400,000 liability with no adjustment until the contingency is finally resolved","Reduce the contingent consideration liability and credit $500,000 to additional paid-in capital"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under ASC 805-30-35, contingent consideration classified as a liability is remeasured at fair value each reporting period, with changes recognized in earnings. The $500,000 decrease from $1,400,000 to $900,000 is reported as a gain in the current period.
Wrong (A): Goodwill adjustments for contingent consideration are only permitted during the measurement period for acquisition-date conditions, not post-acquisition fair value changes.
