  choices = $EXPL$["$865, because the effective interest method applies a constant market rate to a declining carrying amount","$865, because the stated coupon rate decreases each year as the bond premium is amortized","$14,420, because premium amortization fully replaces interest expense recognition over time","$0, because interest expense remains constant each period under the effective interest method"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under ASC 835-30-35, the effective interest method applies the market rate (6%) to the carrying amount each period. As premium amortization reduces the carrying amount, interest expense declines: Year 1 $125,580 minus Year 2 $124,715 equals $865.
